steps:
Add this site to the Caddyfile, put the hash in place of HASH, then reload Caddy.
:2020 {
basic_auth {
dumbmonit HASH
}
@readonly {
method GET
path /config/apps/http/servers /reverse_proxy/upstreams /metrics
}
handle @readonly {
reverse_proxy localhost:2019 {
header_up Host localhost:2019
}
}
respond 403
}

Give it the server-wide read rights it needs to see the state of the engine, and nothing else.
GRANT VIEW SERVER STATE TO dumbmonit;
GRANT VIEW ANY DEFINITION TO dumbmonit;

Optional, for the SQL Server Agent jobs: let it read the job history in msdb.
USE msdb;
CREATE USER dumbmonit FOR LOGIN dumbmonit;
ALTER ROLE SQLAgentReaderRole ADD MEMBER dumbmonit;

Add this location to the server block Nginx already serves, restricted to the DumbMonit host (adjust the address).
location /basic_status {
stub_status;
allow 10.0.0.5;
deny all;
}

As a privileged user, create the account DumbMonit will use, with the two rights it needs.
CREATE USER dumbmonit IDENTIFIED BY "choose-a-long-password";
GRANT CREATE SESSION, SELECT_CATALOG_ROLE TO dumbmonit;
